---
/**
 * How it works — the platform behind the sites.
 *
 * Everything on this page is checked against the shipped client portal
 * (GetYourWebsiteAdmin, `development`, the `client/` workspace) rather than
 * written from the pitch. Where a capability has a condition attached — a
 * custom domain needs the maintenance plan, only approved versions can be
 * hosted — the condition is on the page. The voice rule for this site is plain
 * and specific, and a capability with its limits stated reads as more credible
 * than one without.
 *
 * Deliberately NOT claimed here: no superlatives, no invented statistics, and
 * the only third-party figures are Cloudflare's own published ones, quoted with
 * a link so a visitor can check them. No Cloudflare logo, no implication of
 * partnership or endorsement — we are a customer of theirs, like anyone else.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../data/url.js';
import { LIVE_SITE_URL } from '../data/site.js';

const pagespeed = `https://pagespeed.web.dev/analysis?url=${encodeURIComponent(LIVE_SITE_URL)}`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How it works"
  description="Every revision is a saved version you can put live with one button. Managed hosting and domains, a build process with a human at the end of it, and your photos dragged straight onto the page."
>
  <!-- 1. Intro ---------------------------------------------------------- -->
  <section class="section section--dark has-stars has-glow section--tight">
    <div class="shell-narrow">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">The platform</p>
        <h1>A website you can actually run.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Most of what you're paying for isn't the first version of the site. It's
          what happens for the two years after it — changing it, hosting it,
          keeping it yours. Here's how that part works.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. Versioning — the lead ------------------------------------------- -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Versions</p>
        <h2>Every change is saved as a new version. Nothing is overwritten.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Send us a batch of changes and a person reads them, builds them, and
          gives you back a new version of your site. The old one doesn't go
          anywhere. You can add photos to the new version and put it live
          independently of every version that came before it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-3" data-reveal-group>
        <article class="card" data-reveal>
          <h3>You ask in plain words</h3>
          <p>
            Click any part of your site and say what you want changed. No file
            names, no "third paragraph, second sentence".
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-reveal>
          <h3>A person builds it</h3>
          <p>
            Not an automatic find-and-replace. Someone reads the request, makes
            the change, and checks it before it reaches you.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-reveal>
          <h3>You get a new version</h3>
          <p>
            Saved alongside the others, with its own photos. The portal draws
            them as a tree, so you can see what came from what.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. The one-button switch — the strongest thing we have -------------- -->
  <section class="section section--dark has-stars has-glow">
    <div class="shell-narrow">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">The part people don't expect</p>
        <h2>You choose which version is live. It's one button.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="stack-6" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">
          In November you ask for something more Christmassy. We build it, you
          approve it, you press host — and that's your site until you decide
          otherwise. In January you press host on the version from before, and
          you're back to normal. The Christmas one is still sitting there.
        </p>
        <p class="lead">
          Next November you press one button. You build the seasonal version
          once and reuse it every year.
        </p>
        <p>
          Two honest details. Only versions we've reviewed and approved can be
          put live — that's what stops a half-finished draft reaching your
          customers. And if a version still has empty photo slots, the portal
          tells you how many before it lets you go ahead.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4. Hosting and domains --------------------------------------------- -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Hosting and domains</p>
        <h2>You never touch a registrar or a DNS record.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Search for a domain in your portal, pick one, and press connect. We
          register it in your business's name and point it at your site. There
          is no control panel to learn and no nameserver to copy and paste.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-2" data-reveal-group>
        <article class="card" data-reveal>
          <h3>Fast where your customers are</h3>
          <p>
            Your site is served from Cloudflare's network. Cloudflare publishes
            its own numbers for that network: hundreds of cities across 100+
            countries, and within about 50 milliseconds of roughly 95% of the
            Internet-connected population. You don't have to take our word for
            any of it —
            <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/network/" rel="noopener">
              their network page
            </a>
            is public.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-reveal>
          <h3>What that means for you</h3>
          <p>
            Someone looking you up on their phone down the road gets the site
            quickly, and it stays up when you're busy. That's the whole of the
            benefit — we're not going to dress it up as anything more.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <p class="rule" data-reveal></p>
      <p data-reveal>
        <strong>The condition, stated plainly:</strong> connecting a custom
        domain comes with the maintenance plan, and we need your business
        contact details first because the domain is registered in that name.
        Without it your site still lives at a web address we give you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5. How the sites are made ------------------------------------------- -->
  <section class="section section--dark has-stars">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">How they're made</p>
        <h2>It isn't one prompt into a chatbot.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          We'd rather tell you what actually happens than claim our sites are
          the best ones out there. Judge the process.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ol class="steps" data-reveal-group>
        <li data-reveal>
          <span class="steps__n" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
          <div>
            <h3>We research your business first</h3>
            <p>
              Your listing, your reviews, what you actually sell, and how other
              businesses in your industry present themselves — before a single
              page is drafted.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li data-reveal>
          <span class="steps__n" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
          <div>
            <h3>It's built from curated pieces</h3>
            <p>
              Component libraries we maintain, rather than a layout invented
              from scratch every time. That's why the sites hold together.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li data-reveal>
          <span class="steps__n" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Several passes, not one</h3>
            <p>
              Specialised agents draft the site, critique the draft, and refine
              it — each one doing a narrow job well instead of one model trying
              to do everything at once.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li data-reveal>
          <span class="steps__n" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
          <div>
            <h3>A person signs it off</h3>
            <p>
              Every site is reviewed by one of us before you see it. Nothing
              reaches a client unlooked at.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6. Images and assets ------------------------------------------------ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Your photos</p>
        <h2>Drag them onto the page and save.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Your site has photo slots. Open the image panel, drag one of your
          photos onto a slot, and save it. No emailing us files, no naming
          things <code>hero-image-final-v2.jpg</code>, no waiting on us to do it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-2" data-reveal-group>
        <article class="card" data-reveal>
          <h3>A library that stays yours</h3>
          <p>
            Upload once and reuse across versions. Photos are converted to a
            modern format on the way in, so they stay sharp without slowing the
            page down.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-reveal>
          <h3>Hosted with the site</h3>
          <p>
            We store and serve your images from our own asset host, on the same
            fast network as the site itself. It's one less account for you to
            keep track of.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 7. Performance proof ------------------------------------------------ -->
  <section class="section section--dark has-stars has-glow">
    <div class="shell-narrow">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Don't take our word for it</p>
        <h2>Run the test yourself.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Google publishes a free tool that grades any public web page on four
          things. We've prefilled it with this site — the one you're reading
          right now — so you can run it against us without asking us anything.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="scorecard" data-reveal-group>
        <li data-reveal>Performance</li>
        <li data-reveal>Accessibility</li>
        <li data-reveal>Best Practices</li>
        <li data-reveal>SEO</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="btn-row btn-row--center" data-reveal>
        <a class="btn btn--gold btn--lg" href={pagespeed} rel="noopener">
          Run the test yourself
        </a>
      </div>

      <p class="scorecard__note" data-reveal>
        We deliberately haven't printed a score here. Real results move between
        runs — a single slow image is enough to shift one — and a number we
        typed ourselves would be worth less than a test you ran.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 8. CTA -------------------------------------------------------------- -->
  <section class="section section--dark has-stars has-glow cta-band">
    <div class="shell-narrow" style="text-align:center" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="cta-band__title">See it with your own business in it.</h2>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-inline:auto">
        We'll build you a free mockup of your homepage first. No commitment, no
        card, no catch.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row btn-row--center" style="margin-top:var(--s-5)">
        <a class="btn btn--gold btn--lg" href={url('/contact')}>Request a free mockup</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href={url('/demo')}>Try the client demo</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Numbered process list. The number is a gold chip so the sequence reads at a
     glance without turning into a decorative timeline. */
  .steps {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-4);
    margin-top: var(--s-6);
  }

  .steps li {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--s-4);
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .steps__n {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 2.1rem;
    height: 2.1rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: var(--gold-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--gold-line);
    color: var(--gold);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .steps h3 { margin-bottom: var(--s-1); }

  @media (min-width: 860px) {
    .steps { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--s-6) var(--s-7); }
  }

  /* The four Lighthouse categories, named but never scored — see the note in
     the markup for why there is no number here. */
  .scorecard {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--s-2);
    margin: var(--s-6) 0 var(--s-5);
  }

  .scorecard li {
    padding: 0.5rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-dark);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: rgba(230, 231, 235, 0.04);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-label);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--silver-light);
  }

  .scorecard__note {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: var(--s-5) auto 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--t-small);
    color: var(--silver);
  }

  .rule {
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--line-dark);
    margin: var(--s-6) 0 var(--s-4);
  }
</style>
